WebKit: LayerTreeHostPlayStation builds with the Skia painting engine.

SkiaPaintingEngine::create takes the GPU context's thread-safe proxy since the
GTK and WPE ports moved to Ganesh DDL painting; the PlayStation layer tree host
(whose Skia path no port builds at this revision, the PlayStation port still
uses Cairo) calls it with no arguments. A null proxy is "no GPU context", which
is what a CPU-only port has. The composited path is compiled for
USE_COORDINATED_GRAPHICS and never entered (acceleratedCompositingEnabled is
false).

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHostPlayStation.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHostPlayStation.cpp
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 #if USE(CAIRO)
     , m_paintingEngine(Cairo::PaintingEngine::create())
 #elif USE(SKIA)
-    , m_skiaPaintingEngine(SkiaPaintingEngine::create())
+    , m_skiaPaintingEngine(SkiaPaintingEngine::create({ }))
 #endif
 {
     {
